Phase OS-11: Kernel Network Application Layer - 3 new kernel ASM modules:

1. kernel/net_dns.asm (DNS Resolver)
   - AArch64 ASM implementation of DNS client (RFC 1035)
   - Query construction: standard A (IPv4), AAAA (IPv6), MX, TXT, CNAME, NS, PTR record types
   - Response parsing: answer section extraction, TTL tracking, authoritative/recursive flags
   - Cache: 256 entries (name→IP), TTL-based expiration, LRU eviction
   - Resolver: iterative resolution with up to 3 nameservers (configurable)
   - Message format: 12-byte header, question/answer/authority/additional sections
   - Reverse lookup: IP→name via in-addr.arpa / ip6.arpa
   - Export symbols: net_dns_init, net_dns_resolve, net_dns_reverse, net_dns_cache_add, net_dns_set_server
   - Integration: uses net_udp.asm port 53 for transport

2. kernel/net_http.asm (HTTP/1.1 Client & Server)
   - AArch64 ASM implementation of HTTP protocol (RFC 7230-7235)
   - Client: GET/POST/PUT/DELETE methods, header parsing, chunked transfer encoding
   - Server: request dispatch, status codes (200/301/400/404/500), response building
   - Connection management: keep-alive (max 16 persistent connections), timeout
   - URL parser: scheme/host/port/path/query/fragment extraction
   - Header table: 64 headers max per request/response, common header name lookup
   - Content negotiation: Accept, Content-Type (text/html, application/json, text/plain)
   - Cookie support: Set-Cookie parsing, Cookie header construction (32 cookies)
   - Export symbols: net_http_init, net_http_get, net_http_post, net_http_listen, net_http_respond
   - Integration: uses net_tcp.asm for transport, net_tls.asm for HTTPS

3. kernel/net_ws.asm (WebSocket Protocol)
   - AArch64 ASM implementation of WebSocket (RFC 6455)
   - Handshake: HTTP upgrade, Sec-WebSocket-Key/Accept (SHA-1 + base64)
   - Frame parsing: opcode (text/binary/close/ping/pong), mask handling, payload extraction
   - Frame building: client→server (masked), server→client (unmasked)
   - Fragmentation: continuation frames, max message size (64KB)
   - Ping/pong: keepalive with automatic pong response
   - Connection state: CONNECTING/OPEN/CLOSING/CLOSED (4 states)
   - Max 32 simultaneous WebSocket connections
   - Export symbols: net_ws_init, net_ws_connect, net_ws_accept, net_ws_send, net_ws_recv, net_ws_close
   - Integration: uses net_http.asm for upgrade handshake, net_tcp.asm for transport

All modules follow existing kernel conventions (.arch armv8-a, .global exports, stp/ldp frame setup).
